rate fluctuation resulted in an increase of $741,000 and $546,000 in total revenue during the fiscal years ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively.</p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:12pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;">44</span></p></div></div>
